# CAT1b: If an asystole alarm occurs when an invasive blood pressure sensor
# is present without alarms on that sensing pathway, it may be flagged as
# likely false positive.
#
# Matches on the metric's own identity + rate (metric:HeartRate, hasRate
# metricRate:Absent) rather than on physiologicalProcess:CardiacContraction —
# tightened once a real "PHILIPSMONITOR - Asystolie" archetype became
# available (p75 corpus tier; see EVALUATION/MDA-POC/cat_rules_report.md).
# An earlier version matched on CardiacContraction alone, before that
# archetype existed to match precisely against — which would ALSO have
# fired for "PHILIPSMONITOR - HF hoog"/"Lage hartfreq." (any HeartRate-
# derived alarm reaches the same process), a real over-match risk against
# actual results, not just a cosmetic imprecision. metric:HeartRate +
# hasRate Absent is exactly what "PHILIPSMONITOR - Asystolie" carries and
# nothing else in the corpus currently does.
#
# "An IBP sensor is present" can only be detected through an alarm that has
# itself revealed that pathway at some point in this patient's history — no
# independent device inventory exists in this framework (see
# mda_poc_assessment.py's background_graph(kb, past, identity) — the
# patient's full structural history so far, not just what is currently
# revealing, is exactly what makes this fire for a pathway that alarmed
# once and then stopped, rather than never at all). Documented, not worked
# around: an inventory concept independent of alarm history is CAT3-
# adjacent scope, deliberately deferred.
#
# ?alarm is pre-bound by assess.py. mda:triggeredBy points directly at the
# arriving alarm's own FunctionalUnit particular (assess.py's
# add_triggered_by — no mda:hasFunctionalUnit hop needed from it), the same
# fix cat2b_metric_sensor.rq's header explains in full. The
# ?ibpDevice -> mda:hasFunctionalUnit -> ?ibpFunctionalUnit hop below is a
# genuine device-level fan-out query ("does this device have an IBP FU at
# all, ever"), not per-alarm, so it is unaffected and left as-is.
#
# Validated against DATA/CAT_evaluation/cat1b_pos (an IBP alarm ends long
# before the asystole arrives — still structurally known, fires) and
# cat1b_neg (the IBP alarm is still active when the asystole arrives —
# correctly does not fire). See cat_rules_report.md for the full case.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX metric: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric/>
PREFIX metricRate: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-rate/>
PREFIX functionalUnit: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/functional-unit/>

SELECT ?ibpFunctionalUnit WHERE {
  ?alarm mda:hasMessage ?msg .
  ?msg mda:concernsPatient ?patient .
  ?msg mda:triggeredBy/mda:hasSensor/mda:sensorProducesSignal/
       mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric ?metric .
  ?metric a metric:HeartRate .
  ?metric mda:hasRate metricRate:Absent .

  ?patient mda:isMonitoredBy ?ibpDevice .
  ?ibpDevice mda:hasFunctionalUnit ?ibpFunctionalUnit .
  ?ibpFunctionalUnit a functionalUnit:FU_InvasiveBloodPressure .

  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?otherAlarm mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy ?ibpFunctionalUnit .
  }
}
